The cytoplasmic membrane depolarization assay was performed using the membrane-potential-sensitive dye DiSC3-5. A. baumannii ATCC 19606 in the mid-logarithmic phase were washed and resuspended at 0.05 OD ml−1 (optical value at 600 nm) in HEPES buffer (pH 7.2) containing 20 mmol l−1 of glucose and 0.1 mol l−1 of KCl. DiSC3-5 (20 μmol l−1) was added to the bacterial suspension (100 μl per well) for 15 min to stabilize the fluorescence, which indicates the incorporation of the dye into the bacterial membrane, and then the peptides were mixed 1:1 with the bacteria to a final concentration corresponding to their MIC values. Membrane depolarization was then followed by reading changes in the fluorescence (λex = 622 nm, λem = 670 nm) over time for 60 min. The relative fluorescence was calculated using the untreated control (buffer + bacteria + fluorescent dye) and polymyxin B (positive control) as baselines and the following equation was applied to reflect the percentage of difference between the baselines and the sample:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
